      "id": "relative_schedule_time",
      "public_anchor": "\"Schedule it for Wednesday morning\" from public_input.prompt[1].content",
      "kind": "constraint",
      "status": "gap",
      "gap_category": "other:relative_schedule_binding",
      "mechanism_sketch": "The Buffer handler now persists an explicit scheduled_at as due_at, but the public initial state has no reference clock and the relative instruction does not determine a timestamp. Keep due_at/date outcome unknown rather than inventing an absolute time.",
